7. A bank will be considered as fully complying with ECBA if it meets the following conditions, based on the audited financial statements as of 31st March of the immediately preceding financial year:
The CRAR should be at least one percentage point above the minimum CRAR applicable to the bank as on the reference date;
Net NPAs of not more than 3%;
Net profits during the preceding two financial years;
No default in the maintenance of CRR / SLR during the preceding and current financial year till the time of Board resolution declaring the bank as ECBA compliant / application for authorization;
Core Banking Solution (CBS) fully implemented; and

